hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"6","What has come regarding ablution. Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Dimashqi Abu al-Jumahir narrated to us that Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to them; Sharik ibn Abi Namir narrated to me, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wash his face with his right hand."
"7","Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad informed us, from Ishaq ibn Suwayd, from al-Ala ibn Ziyad, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he performed the ritual bath, then saw a spot on his shoulder that the water had not reached, so he took a lock of hair from his head, squeezed it over his shoulder, then wiped his hand over that spot."
"8","Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Za'idah informed us, Hisham narrated to us, from Hafsah bint Sirin, from Abu al-Aliyah, who said: A man with impaired eyesight came and entered the mosque while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying with his Companions; he stumbled into a pit that was in the mosque, and a group of them laughed. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the prayer, he ordered whoever had laughed among them to repeat the ablution and repeat the prayer. Abu Dawud said: This report was narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through al-Hasan, Ibrahim, and al-Zuhri, and all of their outlets go back to Abu al-Aliyah. Ibrahim narrated it from Abu Hashim al-Rummani, and al-Zuhri narrated it from Sulayman ibn Arqam, from al-Hasan. And Hafs al-Minqari said: I am the one who narrated it to al-Hasan from Abu al-Aliyah."
"9","Muhammad ibn al-Ala and Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, both saying: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, who said: A group from Banu Qushayr came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we travel in the land with our families, and we have no water with us except enough for our lips; may one of us be intimate with his wife? He said: Yes, even if it be for up to two years."
"10","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, al-Layth informed us, from Uqayl, from al-Zuhri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) found blood on his garment and withdrew from prayer."
"11","Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Jarir - meaning Ibn Hazim - narrated to us; I heard Abd al-Malik - meaning Ibn Umayr - narrating from Abdullah ibn Ma'qil ibn Muqarrin, who said: A Bedouin stood in a corner of the mosque, uncovered himself and urinated there. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take the soil he urinated upon, throw it away, and pour water over its place. Abu Dawud said: It has been narrated with a connected chain, but it is not authentic."
